&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The whole &lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/components/category/mobile" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Mobile category&lt;/a&gt; has 15 components, all built to these rules, with reduced motion support and designed light and dark themes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


How do you test mobile-first React components?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Test at 390 by 844 and 360 by 780 with touch enabled, then on a real iPhone for the parts emulators get wrong. Chrome's device mode switches the pointer to coarse, which is enough to see &lt;code&gt;pointer-coarse&lt;/code&gt; styles and the sheets. It does not reproduce the iOS keyboard, the focus zoom, the home indicator or the toolbar resizing, so those need a phone.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For automated checks, Playwright can emulate a touch phone per test file:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;expect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;test&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;@playwright/test&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nx"&gt;test&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;use&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;viewport&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;width&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;390&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;height&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;844&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;hasTouch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;isMobile&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;test&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;filters open as a bottom sheet on a phone&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;page&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;goto&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;/listings&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;getByRole&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Filters&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;tap&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;expect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;getByRole&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;dialog&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Filters&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;toBeVisible&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Run the same pass in light and dark and with reduced motion turned on. A sheet handle or a hairline drawn at a low opacity can be clear in one theme and vanish in the other, and under reduced motion every overlay still has to open and close, only with a shorter slide or a fade.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Which guides go deeper on each rule?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Each of these posts in &lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/blog/category/mobile-ui" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Mobile UI in React&lt;/a&gt; takes one rule or one component further:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/blog/shadcn-responsive-dialog-on-mobile" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Shadcn responsive dialog&lt;/a&gt;: a centered card on desktop and a bottom sheet on phones, with the content written once.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/blog/react-bottom-sheet-for-the-web" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;React bottom sheet for the web&lt;/a&gt;: snap points, drag to dismiss, nested sheets and the keyboard on vaul.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/blog/minimum-touch-target-size-react-tailwind" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Minimum touch target size&lt;/a&gt;: the WCAG, iOS and Android numbers, and 44px on touch in Tailwind without a bloated desktop.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/blog/tailwind-safe-area-insets" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Tailwind safe area insets&lt;/a&gt;: bottom bars, FABs and toasts clear of the notch and the home indicator.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/blog/100vh-mobile-dvh-tailwind" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;100vh on mobile&lt;/a&gt;: when to use dvh, svh or lvh, and full-height shells that do not jump.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/blog/react-bottom-navigation-bar" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;React bottom navigation bar&lt;/a&gt;: a tab bar with badges, a center action and hide on scroll.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/blog/react-pull-to-refresh" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;React pull to refresh&lt;/a&gt;: a custom refresh in a PWA that does not fight the browser's own.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/blog/web-vibration-api-haptic-feedback" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Web Vibration API&lt;/a&gt;: the haptic feedback a page can trigger on Android and iPhone.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/blog/react-pwa-install-prompt" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;React PWA install prompt&lt;/a&gt;: an install prompt for Chrome, Edge and iPhone, and when not to ask.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/blog/responsive-table-mobile-cards" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Responsive tables on mobile&lt;/a&gt;: when rows become cards, which columns survive, and sorting and bulk actions without headers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/blog/react-segmented-control" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;React segmented control&lt;/a&gt;: the iOS thumb you can drag, radio semantics, and when tabs or a toggle group fit better.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/blog/react-wheel-picker" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;React wheel picker&lt;/a&gt;: iOS wheels for times and dates on a native snapping scroller, with a typed field on desktop.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Where should you start?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Start with the overlays, because they are the most visible mobile failure and the cheapest to fix. Install the free Popover with &lt;code&gt;npx wingo-ui@latest add popover&lt;/code&gt; (it brings the Drawer, the Button and the media query hook along), swap it in for one panel that people open on phones, and try it on your own device. The tab bar, sticky CTA bar, pull to refresh, haptic button and data table are part of &lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/pricing" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Wingo UI Pro&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Components in this post
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/components/drawer" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Drawer&lt;/a&gt; (Free): The library's bottom sheet on vaul: drag to dismiss, snap points, nesting, and a side panel or dialog on desktop. Install: &lt;code&gt;npx wingo-ui@latest add drawer&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/components/popover" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Popover&lt;/a&gt; (Free): Rich floating content anchored to a trigger, like a quick filter, form or share panel, that becomes a bottom sheet on phones. Install: &lt;code&gt;npx wingo-ui@latest add popover&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/components/bottom-tab-bar" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Bottom Tab Bar&lt;/a&gt; (Pro): The phone's primary navigation: 3 to 5 tabs at the thumb with an animated pill, badges, a raised center action and hide on scroll. Install: &lt;code&gt;npx wingo-ui@latest add bottom-tab-bar&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/components/pull-to-refresh" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Pull To Refresh&lt;/a&gt; (Pro): Pull a list down past its top to reload it, with rubberband resistance, an arrow, iOS spokes or a Material ring, and a haptic tick. Install: &lt;code&gt;npx wingo-ui@latest add pull-to-refresh&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/components/sticky-cta-bar" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Sticky CTA Bar&lt;/a&gt; (Pro): The bottom action bar of product, listing and checkout pages on phones: the price on one side, the main action on the other. Install: &lt;code&gt;npx wingo-ui@latest add sticky-cta-bar&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/components/data-table" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Data Table&lt;/a&gt; (Pro): The admin table on TanStack Table v9: search, filters, sorting, bulk actions, pinning, resizing, virtualization and cards on phones. Install: &lt;code&gt;npx wingo-ui@latest add data-table&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/components/haptic-button" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Haptic Button&lt;/a&gt; (Pro): A button that answers like a native control: spring press, touch ripple, a haptic tick, a long-press action and a hold-to-confirm mode. Install: &lt;code&gt;npx wingo-ui@latest add haptic-button&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


FAQ
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


What is a mobile-first React component?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A component designed for touch, a narrow screen and an on-screen keyboard first, then enhanced for a mouse and a wide window. On a phone it changes its behavior as well as its layout: it opens a bottom sheet instead of a popover, keeps 44px hit areas and has no hover-only controls.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


How big should buttons be in a mobile web app?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;WCAG 2.2 asks for 24 by 24 CSS pixels at level AA and 44 by 44 at level AAA. Apple's guidelines use 44 by 44 points as the default iOS control size and Android recommends 48 by 48 dp. A practical rule for the web is 44px on coarse pointers with 8px between targets.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Should I use a useIsMobile hook or CSS media queries?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Use CSS breakpoints for anything visible on the first paint, because the server cannot know the screen width and a hook returns a guess there. Use the hook for behavior that starts after an interaction, such as opening a bottom sheet instead of a popover.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Does shadcn/ui have a bottom sheet for mobile?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Yes, the Drawer. As of October 2026 its Base UI version is built on Base UI's drawer and its Radix version on Vaul, and the docs show a responsive example that renders a Dialog on desktop and a Drawer on mobile. Popover, Select and Dropdown Menu do not switch to a sheet on their own.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Why do hover effects not work on phones?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Touch screens have no hover, and in Tailwind CSS v4 the hover variant only applies when the primary input can hover, so a control that only appears on hover never shows up on a phone. Reveal it on focus and on coarse pointers as well, or replace the hover with a tap or a long press.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Which Wingo UI mobile components are free?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The Drawer, Sheet, Popover, Dialog, Select, Dropdown Menu, Segmented Control, Button and the useMediaQuery hook are free, and the Popover, Dialog, Select and Dropdown Menu open as bottom sheets below 768px by default. The 15 components of the Mobile category (tab bar, sticky CTA bar, pull to refresh, haptic button and more) and the Data Table are Pro.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This article was originally published on the Wingo UI blog: &lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/blog/mobile-first-react-components" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Mobile-First React Components: 9 Rules With Code&lt;/a&gt;. The original has the live, interactive demos and is kept up to date.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I have used VLC Media Player for as long as I can remember. It is arguably the most reliable piece of software on the planet, throw a corrupted 2004 &lt;code&gt;.avi&lt;/code&gt; file at it, and it will play it without flinching.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Yet, every time I open it on a modern display, the UI feels like a relic from the Windows XP era. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Electron-based alternatives look gorgeous, but they consume 600MB of RAM just to open an empty window. I wanted the best of both worlds: &lt;strong&gt;native speed, zero bloat, and a modern aesthetic.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So I spent the last few months rebuilding the media player experience from scratch.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F9tq8c50w65nt4layhzkk.png" alt=" " width="800" height="437"&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


The Architecture: Tauri v2 + Rust + React 19
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The core constraint was memory and responsiveness. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Instead of bundling Chromium (Electron), I chose &lt;strong&gt;Tauri v2&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Backend (Rust)&lt;/strong&gt;: Handles low-level file I/O, IPC pipelines, and OS-level window management. Tauri's memory footprint hovers around 30–45MB.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Frontend (React 19 + TypeScript)&lt;/strong&gt;: Renders a fluid, frosted-glass Canvas HUD with auto-hiding controls, visual chapter scrubbers, and instant keyboard shortcuts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Audio Processing&lt;/strong&gt;: A dedicated 10-band graphic equalizer with pre-amplification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


What I Learned About Frame-Accurate Scrubbing
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The hardest part was building a seekbar that didn't feel stuttery. Most web-based players trigger a re-render on every &lt;code&gt;timeupdate&lt;/code&gt; event (approx. 4 times per second), causing the scrub head to snap awkwardly. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;By separating the &lt;strong&gt;rendering timeline&lt;/strong&gt; from the &lt;strong&gt;underlying media buffer&lt;/strong&gt; with an interpolated RAF (RequestAnimationFrame) loop, scrubbing feels buttery smooth even with high-bitrate 4K files.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Try It Out
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The project is open source under the MIT license, and I've published pre-built binaries for Linux:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;GitHub Repository&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;a href="https://github.com/shahaayush265/vlcreborn" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;shahaayush265/vlcreborn&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Live Binary Releases&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;a href="https://github.com/shahaayush265/vlcreborn/releases/tag/v1.0.0" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;v1.0.0 Release&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you build desktop apps or love media playback systems, I'd love your thoughts and pull requests!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Originally published on &lt;a href="https://coremesh.online/cannot-read-properties-of-undefined-reading-bind/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;CoreMesh&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'bind')&lt;/code&gt; means your code ran &lt;code&gt;something.bind(...)&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;something&lt;/code&gt; was &lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt; at that moment. The word in quotes is the property the engine tried to read, and &lt;code&gt;bind&lt;/code&gt; is a method that only exists on functions. So the real bug is one step to the left of &lt;code&gt;.bind&lt;/code&gt;: the function you expected to be there isn't. Usually it's a typo in a method name, a method defined on the wrong object, or a handler that hasn't been assigned yet when the binding runs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The fix is to find out what that left-hand expression actually is, then either make sure it's defined (most common), guard it, or use optional chaining so the missing case is handled on purpose. The sections below walk through those in order, from the most direct fix to the defensive patterns for async code.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What the error means
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here's the full message as V8 (Chrome, Edge, Node.js) prints it. Firefox and Safari word it differently, as the &lt;a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Errors/Cant_access_property" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;MDN page on this TypeError&lt;/a&gt; lists:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'bind')      (V8: Chrome, Edge, Node.js)
TypeError: "x" is undefined                                           (Firefox)
TypeError: undefined is not an object (evaluating 'obj.x')           (Safari)
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Read it as three parts:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Cannot read properties of undefined&lt;/strong&gt; tells you the object on the left of the dot was &lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt;. If it says &lt;code&gt;null&lt;/code&gt; instead, same problem, different nullish value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;(reading 'bind')&lt;/strong&gt; tells you which property was being read. It does not mean &lt;code&gt;bind&lt;/code&gt; is broken. It means the thing you called &lt;code&gt;bind&lt;/code&gt; on doesn't exist.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The stack trace&lt;/strong&gt; underneath points to the file and line. That line contains the &lt;code&gt;.bind(&lt;/code&gt; you need to look at.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;MDN sums up the cause in one sentence: there was an unexpected type, most often an &lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;null&lt;/code&gt; value. You can't invoke a method on either of those. The engine doesn't know what you meant to bind, so it stops.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Find the undefined object behind 'bind'
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Go to the line from the stack trace and split the expression at the last dot before &lt;code&gt;bind&lt;/code&gt;. Everything to the left is the suspect.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;handleClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;bind&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;       &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// suspect: this.handleClick&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;service&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;api&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;request&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;bind&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;service&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// suspect: service.api.request&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;handlers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;].&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;bind&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ctx&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;          &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// suspect: handlers[name]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Then check what the suspect evaluates to at that point. Three quick ways:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Log it before the bind.&lt;/strong&gt; A &lt;code&gt;console.log(this.handleClick)&lt;/code&gt; on the line above is crude, but it answers the question in one reload.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Set a breakpoint on the line&lt;/strong&gt; in your browser's DevTools or in Node's inspector and hover the expression.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Search the file for the exact name.&lt;/strong&gt; If &lt;code&gt;handleClick&lt;/code&gt; is only mentioned once, the method was never defined and you've found your typo.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;While you're there, work out why it's undefined. The common reasons are:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Cause&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;What it looks like&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Misspelled method name&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;this.handleClik.bind(this)&lt;/code&gt; when the method is &lt;code&gt;handleClick&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Method defined on another class or module&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Binding &lt;code&gt;this.submit&lt;/code&gt; in a component that never declares &lt;code&gt;submit&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Method is an arrow property or static, not where you think&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;static format()&lt;/code&gt; bound as &lt;code&gt;this.format&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Wrong key in a lookup&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;handlers[action]&lt;/code&gt; where &lt;code&gt;action&lt;/code&gt; is &lt;code&gt;"SAVE"&lt;/code&gt; but the key is &lt;code&gt;"save"&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Object not loaded yet&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Binding a method from data that arrives later from &lt;code&gt;fetch&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Destructuring that missed&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;const { onSave } = props&lt;/code&gt; when the parent never passed &lt;code&gt;onSave&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The last two are the async cases, and they get their own section below.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Fix 1: define the function or correct the name
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If the suspect should always exist, the right fix is to make it exist. Don't paper over a typo with a guard. Here's the most common shape of this bug in a class, followed by its fix:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;class&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;constructor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;try&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Typo: the class has no method called handleClik&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;handleClik&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;bind&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;catch &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;err&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;log&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Caught:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;err&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Correct name, same line otherwise&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;handleClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;bind&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;handleClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;clicked, this is a &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;constructor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;log&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;());&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The first attempt throws because &lt;code&gt;this.handleClik&lt;/code&gt; is &lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt;. The second works because the name matches the declared method. In a React class component the pattern is identical: every &lt;code&gt;this.x.bind(this)&lt;/code&gt; in the constructor needs a matching &lt;code&gt;x() {}&lt;/code&gt; in the class body.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How to confirm it worked:&lt;/strong&gt; the error disappears and the bound function actually runs. If you fixed a typo, search the codebase for the misspelled name once more, because the same typo often appears in two places.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you'd rather not bind at all, a class field written as an arrow function keeps &lt;code&gt;this&lt;/code&gt; without a &lt;code&gt;bind&lt;/code&gt; call:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;class&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;handleClick&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;That removes the &lt;code&gt;.bind(&lt;/code&gt; line entirely, which removes the place the error could be thrown.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Fix 2: guard before you bind
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When the function is genuinely optional, such as a plugin hook or a callback a caller may or may not pass, check it first. MDN recommends testing for &lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;null&lt;/code&gt; explicitly:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;hooks&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;onSave&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;undefined&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;hooks&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;onSave&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;save&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;hooks&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;onSave&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;bind&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;For functions I'd go one step further and check the type, because a non-function value with a &lt;code&gt;bind&lt;/code&gt; property is rare but a string or number in the wrong slot is not:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;typeof&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;hooks&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;onSave&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;save&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;hooks&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;onSave&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;bind&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;MDN also notes you can test plain truthiness with &lt;code&gt;if (foo)&lt;/code&gt; when you're sure &lt;code&gt;foo&lt;/code&gt; won't be another falsy value like &lt;code&gt;""&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;0&lt;/code&gt;. For a function slot that's usually safe, but &lt;code&gt;typeof&lt;/code&gt; reads clearer and costs nothing.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How to confirm it worked:&lt;/strong&gt; the error is gone, and when the hook is missing your code takes the branch you intended rather than silently doing nothing. Add a log or a thrown error with a clear message in the &lt;code&gt;else&lt;/code&gt; branch if a missing hook should be a bug.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Fix 3: optional chaining and a default
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Optional chaining (&lt;code&gt;?.&lt;/code&gt;) short-circuits to &lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt; instead of throwing when the thing on its left is &lt;code&gt;null&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt;. It works for property access, bracket access and function calls, per the &lt;a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Operators/Optional_chaining" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;MDN optional chaining reference&lt;/a&gt;. For a bind, you put it between the possibly-missing function and &lt;code&gt;.bind&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;config&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;hooks&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// hooks exists but onSave doesn't: no throw, result is undefined&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;save&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;config&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;hooks&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;onSave&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;bind&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;config&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;log&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;save:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;save&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// plugins doesn't exist at all: chain both steps&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;plugin&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;config&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;plugins&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;onLoad&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;bind&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;config&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;log&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;plugin:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;plugin&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Grouping breaks the short-circuit. This still throws.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;try&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;broken&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;config&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;plugins&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;onLoad&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;bind&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;config&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;log&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;broken&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;catch &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;err&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;log&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;grouped:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;err&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Pair with ?? to supply a fallback function&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;onLoad&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;config&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;plugins&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;onLoad&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;bind&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;config&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;??&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;default loader&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;log&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;onLoad&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;());&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Two details from that example matter in practice:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Every nullable step needs its own &lt;code&gt;?.&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt; If &lt;code&gt;config.plugins&lt;/code&gt; can be missing, &lt;code&gt;config.plugins.onLoad?.bind()&lt;/code&gt; still throws on &lt;code&gt;plugins&lt;/code&gt;. MDN is explicit about this: if the root object itself may be nullish, you have to put &lt;code&gt;?.&lt;/code&gt; at that position as well.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Parentheses end the chain.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;(a?.b).c&lt;/code&gt; evaluates &lt;code&gt;a?.b&lt;/code&gt; to &lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt;, then reads &lt;code&gt;.c&lt;/code&gt; on it and throws. MDN gives exactly this case. Keep the chain unbroken from the nullable step through to &lt;code&gt;.bind&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The nullish coalescing operator (&lt;code&gt;??&lt;/code&gt;) pairs naturally here. &lt;code&gt;fn?.bind(ctx) ?? fallback&lt;/code&gt; gives you a bound function or a default without an &lt;code&gt;if&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How to confirm it worked:&lt;/strong&gt; the line no longer throws, and you've decided what &lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt; means downstream. If callers of &lt;code&gt;save&lt;/code&gt; would themselves crash on &lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt;, you've only moved the error. That's what the &lt;code&gt;??&lt;/code&gt; fallback is for.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Prevent it in async code
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The async version of this bug is the one that passes every test and then fails in production. The function you're binding comes from a response, a lazy import or a store that hasn't populated yet. The code binds it once, early, and that moment is before the data exists.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The rule is simple: don't bind anything that depends on awaited data until after the &lt;code&gt;await&lt;/code&gt;, and validate what came back before you touch it.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;loadHandler&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;registry&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Stand-in for a fetch, dynamic import, or store lookup&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;entry&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Promise&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;resolve&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;registry&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;fn&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;entry&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;handler&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;typeof&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;fn&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;throw&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`No handler registered for "&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;fn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;bind&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;entry&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;registry&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;save&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;save-entry&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;handler&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;saved by &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;loadHandler&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;registry&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;save&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;then&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;run&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;log&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;run&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()));&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;loadHandler&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;registry&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;delete&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;catch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;err&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;log&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;err&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;));&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The missing &lt;code&gt;delete&lt;/code&gt; entry produces an error that names the problem instead of the generic &lt;code&gt;reading 'bind'&lt;/code&gt; message. That's the goal in async code: turn an engine error at an unhelpful line into your own error at the point where the assumption failed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A few more habits that prevent the async flavour:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Bind inside the function that uses the value, not at module load.&lt;/strong&gt; Module-level &lt;code&gt;const run = api.method.bind(api)&lt;/code&gt; executes before any data exists.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;In React, bind or wire handlers in render or in the handler itself&lt;/strong&gt;, not in a constructor that runs before props have arrived. Data fetched in an effect is &lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt; on the first render, so a handler that binds &lt;code&gt;data.callback&lt;/code&gt; has to tolerate that first pass. The same first-render gap causes server and client markup to differ, which is covered in the &lt;a href="https://coremesh.online/hydration-failed-because-the-initial-ui/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;hydration mismatch fix guide&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Check what &lt;code&gt;fetch&lt;/code&gt; actually returned.&lt;/strong&gt; A failed request that your code treated as success leaves &lt;code&gt;response.handler&lt;/code&gt; undefined. If the failure is cross-origin, the browser console will say so, and the &lt;a href="https://coremesh.online/cors-error/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;CORS error header checklist&lt;/a&gt; shows which header is missing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Give destructured callbacks a default.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;const { onSave = () =&amp;gt; {} } = props&lt;/code&gt; means &lt;code&gt;onSave.bind(this)&lt;/code&gt; never sees &lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Same error, different property: 'map', 'length', 'id', '0'
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The word in quotes changes, the diagnosis doesn't. Whatever is left of that property was &lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt;. The table below maps the common variants to what's usually missing.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Message ends with&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Left side was&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Typical cause&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;(reading 'bind')&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;a function&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Misspelled or undeclared method, callback not passed&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;(reading 'map')&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;an array&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;API returned an object or nothing, state not initialized to &lt;code&gt;[]&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;(reading 'length')&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;an array or string&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Same as &lt;code&gt;map&lt;/code&gt;, or a split result on missing text&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;(reading '0')&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;an array&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Indexing &lt;code&gt;rows[0]&lt;/code&gt; when &lt;code&gt;rows&lt;/code&gt; was never set&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;(reading 'id')&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;an object&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Lookup by key missed, item not found, &lt;code&gt;find()&lt;/code&gt; returned &lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;(reading 'split')&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;a string&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Field missing from a record, &lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt; passed where text was expected&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;(reading 'text')&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;an object&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Reading a nested field from an empty or error response&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The fixes are the same three: define the value, guard it, or chain it. For arrays, a default of &lt;code&gt;[]&lt;/code&gt; is the cheapest prevention:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;items&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;items&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;??&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[];&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;items&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;MDN's own example shows the bracket form for array indexes: &lt;code&gt;arr?.[42]&lt;/code&gt; returns &lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt; instead of throwing &lt;code&gt;Cannot read properties of undefined (reading '42')&lt;/code&gt; when &lt;code&gt;arr&lt;/code&gt; is missing.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Common mistakes and gotchas
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fixing the symptom, not the cause.&lt;/strong&gt; Wrapping a required method in &lt;code&gt;?.&lt;/code&gt; makes the error vanish and the feature silently stop working. Use optional chaining only where &lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt; is a legitimate state.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mixing up &lt;code&gt;null&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt; in guards.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;if (fn !== undefined)&lt;/code&gt; lets &lt;code&gt;null&lt;/code&gt; through, and &lt;code&gt;null.bind&lt;/code&gt; throws the same way with &lt;code&gt;null&lt;/code&gt; in the message. Use &lt;code&gt;!= null&lt;/code&gt; (loose), &lt;code&gt;typeof fn === "function"&lt;/code&gt;, or &lt;code&gt;?.&lt;/code&gt;, which handles both.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Expecting &lt;code&gt;?.&lt;/code&gt; to catch non-functions.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;obj.method?.()&lt;/code&gt; returns &lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt; if &lt;code&gt;method&lt;/code&gt; is missing, but if &lt;code&gt;method&lt;/code&gt; is a string, you get &lt;code&gt;obj.method is not a function&lt;/code&gt;. Optional chaining checks for nullish, not for callability.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Using &lt;code&gt;?.&lt;/code&gt; on an undeclared variable.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;undeclaredVar?.prop&lt;/code&gt; throws a &lt;code&gt;ReferenceError&lt;/code&gt;, not &lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt;. Optional chaining only helps once the variable exists.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Assigning through a chain.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;obj?.prop = 1&lt;/code&gt; is a &lt;code&gt;SyntaxError&lt;/code&gt;. Chains are for reading and calling, not writing.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Breaking the chain with parentheses.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;(a?.b).c&lt;/code&gt; throws when &lt;code&gt;a&lt;/code&gt; is nullish. Covered above, but it's the one that surprises people who think they already added the operator.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Binding in a constructor before the data exists.&lt;/strong&gt; The React and async case. The constructor runs once; props and fetched data arrive later.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Blaming the error on a product you're using.&lt;/strong&gt; If you're a user seeing this in a web app or a desktop client rather than a developer writing it, the bug is in that app's JavaScript. Reloading, clearing the cache or updating the app sometimes clears a stale state, but the real fix has to come from the app's developers. Reporting the exact message, including the word in quotes, helps them find it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Quick checklist
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Open the stack trace line and find the &lt;code&gt;.bind(&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Everything left of that dot is the suspect. Log it or hover it in a breakpoint.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Typo or missing method? Fix the name or declare it. Done.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Legitimately optional? Guard with &lt;code&gt;typeof fn === "function"&lt;/code&gt;, or use &lt;code&gt;fn?.bind(ctx)&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Nullable at more than one level? Put &lt;code&gt;?.&lt;/code&gt; at every nullable step and don't wrap any part in parentheses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Need a fallback? Append &lt;code&gt;?? defaultFn&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comes from awaited data? Move the bind after the &lt;code&gt;await&lt;/code&gt; and validate the result before binding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Same message with &lt;code&gt;'map'&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;'length'&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;'0'&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;'id'&lt;/code&gt;? Same steps, default arrays to &lt;code&gt;[]&lt;/code&gt; and objects to &lt;code&gt;{}&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rerun and confirm the bound function actually executes, not just that the error is gone.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


FAQ
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What does cannot read properties of undefined mean?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The value on the left of the dot was undefined, so JavaScript couldn't read the property named in quotes from it. The property name tells you what you tried to read; the fix is to find out why the object before it doesn't exist.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How do I fix cannot read properties of null?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The same way as the undefined version. Null is the other nullish value, and optional chaining (?.) and a typeof check both handle it. If you guard with !== undefined only, null still gets through.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why does this happen in React?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Most often a class constructor binds this.someMethod before that method is declared, or a handler reads props or fetched data on the first render when it's still undefined. Fix the method name, or move the bind after the data arrives and give destructured callbacks a default.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What's the difference between reading 'bind' and reading 'map'?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Only the property that was being read. With 'bind' a function was missing; with 'map' an array was missing. Both mean the thing before the dot was undefined, and both are fixed by defining, guarding or chaining it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;I see this error in an app I use, not in code I wrote. What can I do?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The bug is in that app's JavaScript, so you can't fix it directly. Reloading, clearing the cache or updating to the latest version sometimes clears a stale state; otherwise report the exact message, including the quoted property name, to the app's support.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The original, with any later corrections, is on &lt;a href="https://coremesh.online/cannot-read-properties-of-undefined-reading-bind/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;CoreMesh&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This article was drafted by an AI system, fact-checked against the official sources linked above, and reviewed by a human before publishing.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fkmp7861ftuuxrbxzq5xb.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fkmp7861ftuuxrbxzq5xb.png" alt=" " width="800" height="411"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;As AI models become more integrated into our daily workflows, privacy and local control are rapidly becoming top priorities for developers. Many of us want the power of autonomous AI agents without sending private files, codebases, or API interactions to third-party cloud platforms.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That is why I built &lt;strong&gt;Calabrass&lt;/strong&gt;—a native, local-first personal AI assistant and agent workspace built specifically for Windows.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


💡 What is Calabrass?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Calabrass&lt;/strong&gt; is a single-user, open-source AI desktop application that runs entirely on your machine. It combines a streaming chat interface, an autonomous tool-using agent, workspace file awareness, and a Model Context Protocol (MCP) host—all packaged into a lightweight Windows app.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;No cloud accounts are required, and &lt;strong&gt;no data ever leaves your computer&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


✨ Key Features
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;💬 Streaming Chat &amp;amp; Reasoning UI:&lt;/strong&gt; Real-time token streaming via Server-Sent Events (SSE) with inline rendering for model reasoning/thinking traces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;🤖 Autonomous Agent &amp;amp; Built-in Tools:&lt;/strong&gt; Comes with built-in tools for file reading/writing, shell execution, directory listing, web searching, and URL fetching. Point the agent at a workspace folder, and it executes tasks end-to-end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;🔌 Built-in MCP (Model Context Protocol) Host:&lt;/strong&gt; Easily connect Model Context Protocol servers to extend agent capabilities. Calabrass includes optional bundled servers for Excel automation (&lt;code&gt;excel-mcp&lt;/code&gt;) and Windows desktop control (&lt;code&gt;win-control-mcp&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;🔑 Bring Your Own Keys (BYOK):&lt;/strong&gt; Connect any OpenAI-compatible provider (Groq, Together, local Ollama/vLLM) or Google Gemini via direct API keys saved locally in your isolated SQLite database.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;🗣️ Real-time Voice (Cal Live):&lt;/strong&gt; Speech-to-text integration via Groq Whisper or Mistral for hands-free voice input.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;🔒 100% Data Ownership:&lt;/strong&gt; Your chats, workspace files, logs, and provider configurations stay strictly inside &lt;code&gt;%LOCALAPPDATA%\Calabrass&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


🧱 Architecture &amp;amp; Tech Stack
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Calabrass was designed to be fast, minimal, and fully native:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Layer&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Technology&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Frontend&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;React 19, Vite, Tailwind CSS v4, Base UI, TanStack Router&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Backend&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Go 1.23, SQLite (&lt;code&gt;modernc.org/sqlite&lt;/code&gt;), GoAI SDK, Server-Sent Events&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desktop&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Wails v2 (Native WebView2 window)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Protocol&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Official Go MCP SDK (stdio transport)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;




