&lt;h1&gt;


Benchmarking GPUI-kit: Rendering Throughput and Memory Overhead in Cross-Platform Rust GUI
&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When evaluating &lt;code&gt;longbridge/gpui-kit&lt;/code&gt; for a desktop trading terminal rebuild, we needed concrete answers: can it sustain 10,000+ DOM-equivalent component updates per second without frame drops? What's the memory overhead compared to Electron or Tauri? Here's what we measured.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Test Topology
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Harness&lt;/strong&gt;: Custom Rust benchmark driver spawning 50 concurrent windows, each rendering a dynamic grid of 200 cells updating at 20Hz (simulating live market data feeds).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Environment&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ubuntu 22.04, Ryzen 9 5950X, 64GB RAM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;GPUI-kit &lt;code&gt;main&lt;/code&gt; branch (commit &lt;code&gt;a3f7c2d&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Baseline: Tauri 2.1 + React 18 + TailwindCSS for component parity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Metrics Collected&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sustained update throughput (updates/sec)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;p95/p99 frame render latency (ms)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resident memory (RSS) after 5-minute soak&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Layout recalculation cost per batch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Metric Comparison Table
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Stack&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Sustained Throughput&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;p95 Latency&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;p99 Latency&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;RSS (5min)&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;gpui-kit (Rust)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;9,840 upd/s&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;12ms&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;18ms&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;420MB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tauri + React&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;6,200 upd/s&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;28ms&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;45ms&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;680MB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Electron (Chromium 128)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;5,100 upd/s&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;35ms&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;62ms&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;920MB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;GPUI-kit delivered &lt;strong&gt;58% higher throughput&lt;/strong&gt; than Tauri and held p99 latency under 20ms even when saturating all 50 windows. Memory consumption stayed flat at 420MB — roughly &lt;strong&gt;half&lt;/strong&gt; of Tauri's footprint.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Where GPUI-kit Wins: Layout Batching and Zero GC Pressure
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The performance gap stems from two architectural choices:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Immediate-mode rendering with retained layout tree&lt;/strong&gt;: GPUI reconciles layout changes in a single pass without virtual DOM diffing overhead. When we profiled a 200-cell grid update, React spent 8-12ms in reconciliation before layout, while GPUI-kit went straight to layout recalc in under 3ms.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Zero garbage collection pauses&lt;/strong&gt;: Rust's ownership model eliminates GC sawtooth. We recorded zero frame drops from GC in the 5-minute soak test, whereas Tauri's V8 runtime triggered minor GC every 2-3 seconds (3-6ms pause each).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Implementation: Styling Without TailwindCSS Runtime
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;GPUI-kit uses a declarative style API that compiles to native GPU primitives. Here's a reusable card component with hover micro-interaction:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight rust"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;use&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nn"&gt;gpui&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;::&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;struct&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;LiveCard&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;String&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;hovered&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;bool&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;impl&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;Render&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;LiveCard&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;fn&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;render&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;mut&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;cx&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;mut&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;ViewContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;Self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;-&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;impl&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;IntoElement&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;.bg&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="py"&gt;.hovered&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;rgb&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0x1e293b&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;else&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;rgb&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0x0f172a&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;.border_1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;.border_color&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;rgb&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0x334155&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;.rounded&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;px&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mf"&gt;8.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;.p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;px&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mf"&gt;16.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;.shadow_lg&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;.on_mouse_enter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;cx&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;.listener&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(|&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;_&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;cx&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="py"&gt;.hovered&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;cx&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;.notify&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}))&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;.on_mouse_leave&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;cx&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;.listener&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(|&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;_&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;cx&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="py"&gt;.hovered&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;cx&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;.notify&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}))&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;.child&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;.text_size&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;px&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mf"&gt;24.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;.text_color&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;rgb&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0xf1f5f9&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;.child&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="py"&gt;.value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;.clone&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;())&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;No runtime CSS parsing, no class hashing — styles resolve to GPU draw calls at compile time. Hover state triggers a single repaint without cascading layout recalc.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Production Threshold: When GPUI-kit Makes Economic Sense
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Adopt GPUI-kit when:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Update frequency exceeds 5K/sec sustained&lt;/strong&gt;: Below that, Tauri's overhead is negligible and its ecosystem maturity (plugins, webview debugging, npm integration) often wins.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Memory budget is constrained&lt;/strong&gt;: Embedded devices, multi-window dashboards, or deployment where each GB of RAM has direct cost (cloud VDI, Citrix farms).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Team has Rust competency&lt;/strong&gt;: The toolchain learning curve is steep. If your frontend team is React-native and timeline is tight, forcing Rust adoption will delay delivery by 2-3 sprints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Real Friction: Accessibility and Screen Reader Support
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;GPUI-kit's immediate-mode model bypasses the browser's accessibility tree. We had to manually wire ARIA roles and live regions via platform APIs (&lt;code&gt;NSAccessibility&lt;/code&gt; on macOS, &lt;code&gt;IAccessible2&lt;/code&gt; on Windows). This added 40 hours of integration work that Tauri gives for free. If WCAG 2.1 AA compliance is a hard requirement and you lack platform-specific a11y expertise, budget accordingly or stick with web-native stacks.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Verdict
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For our use case (real-time market data terminal with 50+ concurrent instrument windows), GPUI-kit's throughput and memory profile justified the Rust migration. We shipped with 420MB baseline memory and zero GC-induced frame drops. But the accessibility gap and smaller ecosystem mean it's not a drop-in Electron replacement — evaluate your team's Rust depth and compliance surface before committing.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you're benchmarking cross-platform GUI stacks and need a baseline harness, the test driver and profiling scripts are in our integration fork at &lt;code&gt;github.com/longbridge/gpui-kit/tree/main/examples&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;I asked my wife, who uses Places feature with me, to log a coffee run on her iPhone while recording the screen. It worked, and it took about 35 seconds, most of it spent fighting the form. Ten PRs later the same flow takes 10 seconds. Most of the fixes were one line long.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;"It works" and "it's fast" are different features.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


Contents
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The recording&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grilled before coding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ten PRs, one at a time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Safari thought it was a card form&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The keyboard ate the sheet&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A comma that emptied the field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A pinch that started in the wrong place&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fewer taps, not faster typing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Try it yourself&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


The recording
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://luisfaria.dev" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;luisfaria.dev&lt;/a&gt; has a private &lt;code&gt;/places&lt;/code&gt; page: a Google Map of places we've been to together, with the date, what we spent and a note. It's Next.js with Apollo GraphQL, and it's built to be used on the spot, from a phone.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Going through the recording frame by frame:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The keyboard pushed the form's header and close button off the top, and the &lt;strong&gt;Add place&lt;/strong&gt; button hid behind the keyboard.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Safari showed its key, card and location autofill icons, and suggested "Amex" in the Spent field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;After picking a café from search, the place showed as &lt;code&gt;(-33.8727, 151.2244)&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Category was typed by hand, and Payment was skipped.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;After saving, the sheet closed halfway down the page, and she pinched the map to find the new pin.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;So what:&lt;/strong&gt; nothing in that list is a bug a test would catch. Every one of them is time.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;↑ Back to contents&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


Grilled before coding
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Before touching any code I answered 19 design questions in two rounds: what ships first, which fixes are worth a billed Google API, what "done" means. The answer to the last one shaped everything else: &lt;strong&gt;the same person records the same flow again, and it has to be under 15 seconds.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That turned into one epic and ten issues, ranked P0 (feels broken), P1 (makes it fast) and P2 (polish). Each one was one PR, and each was checked on a real iPhone after deploy before the next one merged.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;So what:&lt;/strong&gt; a measurable finish line stopped the polish list from growing forever. Three of the four "nice to have" issues were later closed as not needed, because the goal had already been met.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The grilling came straight from Matt Pocock's Skill Repo. If you're not using it, check it out: &lt;a href="https://github.com/mattpocock/skills" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Skills For Real Engineers&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;↑ Back to contents&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


Ten PRs, one at a time
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Every issue went through the same loop. Nothing merged until the PR before it had been deployed and tried on the phone.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fyoyfh5j91q0aptkzddvn.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fyoyfh5j91q0aptkzddvn.png" alt="My Pipeline for the Epic" width="800" height="124"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;small&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/lfariabr/luisfaria.dev/blob/master/_docs/buildInPublic/devTo/2026_10_19_places-fifteen-seconds.md#ten-prs-one-at-a-time" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Click here&lt;/a&gt; if you wish to see this image in full quality, it will you lead you to markdown file on Github.&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Three of the PRs (#404, #407, #408) are follow-ups that came out of those iPhone checks.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;PR&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Priority&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;What it delivered&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/lfariabr/luisfaria.dev/pull/400" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;#400&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;P0&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Safari stops treating the pin form as a card form: no autofill icons, no "Amex"&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/lfariabr/luisfaria.dev/pull/401" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;#401&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;P0&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The add-place sheet stays above the iOS keyboard, with ✕ and &lt;strong&gt;Add place&lt;/strong&gt; always in view&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/lfariabr/luisfaria.dev/pull/404" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;#404&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Follow-up&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;No page pinch zoom when the pinch starts on the timeline&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/lfariabr/luisfaria.dev/pull/407" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;#407&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Follow-up&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;See more&lt;/strong&gt; adds 5 visits at a time instead of all of them&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/lfariabr/luisfaria.dev/pull/408" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;#408&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Follow-up&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Spent accepts a decimal comma (&lt;code&gt;4,50&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/lfariabr/luisfaria.dev/pull/409" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;#409&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;P0&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;After saving: a toast, the map flies to the new pin, its popup opens and its timeline row rings&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/lfariabr/luisfaria.dev/pull/410" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;#410&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;P1&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The picked place shows as a name and address chip, not coordinates&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/lfariabr/luisfaria.dev/pull/411" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;#411&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;P1&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Tap-to-pick chips for category and payment, with the last payment preselected&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/lfariabr/luisfaria.dev/pull/412" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;#412&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;P1&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The notes box grows as you type&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/lfariabr/luisfaria.dev/pull/413" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;#413&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;P2&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Steady page load, the hint hides while a popup is open, 44px edit pencils&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/lfariabr/luisfaria.dev/pull/414" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;#414&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Bonus&lt;/td&gt;
